<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Murom</h1><p class="st-meta">1127 CE – 1392 CE (approx.) · capital Murom</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An old principality on the Oka, home of the legend of Peter and Fevronia, later absorbed into Moscow's growing realm.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murom">Murom</a>, named after the Finnic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muroma">Muroma</a> tribe, is mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> under 862. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-the-great">Vladimir I</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-and-gleb">Gleb</a>, later venerated as a saint, held it in the early 11th century. It became the seat of the descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-sviatoslavich">Yaroslav Sviatoslavich</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>, and around 1127 split from the neighbouring <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grand-principality-of-ryazan">Grand Principality of Ryazan</a> to form a separate principality.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murom">Murom</a> was a frontier town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oka-river">Oka</a>, close to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/volga-bulgaria">Volga Bulgaria</a> and the forest peoples, and lived from trade and farming. Its princes were usually overshadowed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vladimir-suzdal">Vladimir-Suzdal</a>. The tale of Prince Peter and the peasant healer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-and-fevronia-of-murom">Fevronia</a>, venerated as patrons of marriage, is set here, as is the epic hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilya-muromets">Ilya Muromets</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murom">Murom</a> in 1239, and it declined into a minor dependent principality. In 1392 Vasily I of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow</a> bought from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> the right to rule Murom along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizhny-novgorod">Nizhny Novgorod</a>, ending its independence.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-murom.jpg" alt="Principality of Murom" width="320" height="257"><figcaption>Image: Hellerick · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Principality_of_Nizhny_Novgorod-Suzdal_14th_century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1127 CE – 1392 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Murom</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gleb, Yaroslav Sviatoslavich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old East Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Murom Principality</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1260&amp;focus=principality-of-murom" aria-label="Principality of Murom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5315 169 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Murom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5635 425L5724 651M5635 425L6352 637M5635 425L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5724 651h0M6352 637h0M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5635 425h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5635 425h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1260&amp;focus=principality-of-murom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
